{
  "_comment": [
    "Pressure language, weighted. The weights are the whole design here.",
    "",
    "The previous implementation treated 'your password' and 'security alert' as",
    "phishing indicators of equal standing to a DMARC failure. Both appear constantly",
    "in legitimate mail - every password-reset confirmation and every real breach",
    "notification contains one - so that list flagged genuine mail as phishing, and",
    "because the old graph skipped the LLM once three rules fired, it did so with no",
    "explanation attached.",
    "",
    "So phrases are graded by how rarely they appear in honest mail:",
    "  0.30-0.45  common in legitimate mail; only meaningful in combination",
    "  0.50-0.65  unusual phrasing, or an odd thing for a real sender to say",
    "  0.70-0.85  a demand that legitimate senders essentially never make",
    "",
    "`scoring` saturates the content category, so quantity cannot substitute for",
    "quality: ten 0.30 phrases still lose to one authentication failure."
  ],
